INT. TAXIDERMY WORKSHOP - EVENING

Glass eyes on every shelf. A stuffed heron guards the doorway. Under a green-shaded lamp, a long worktable holds a half-mounted fox and a ledger.

INSPECTOR AUGUSTINE BELLAMY-OKAFOR (50s, bowler hat, wet umbrella) stands at the table. Opposite him, MISS CLEMENTINE VASQUEZ-HOLT (40s, leather apron, a scalpel in her fist) hovers over the fox. Seated on a stool by the stove are two others: the widow MRS. ODALYS PRENDERGAST (60s, black gloves, a handbag clutched in her lap) and the young apprentice WILFRED TANAKA (19, soot on his cuffs, eyes on the floor).

BELLAMY
Mrs. Prendergast, your husband died on the fourteenth.

MRS. PRENDERGAST
He did.

BELLAMY
And on the fifteenth you commissioned a mounting.

MRS. PRENDERGAST
A cat.

BELLAMY
A cat. Which weighs, according to this ledger, eleven stone.

MISS VASQUEZ
We had to reinforce the frame.

BELLAMY
(to Vasquez)
Did you.

MISS VASQUEZ
It's a very large cat.

BELLAMY
Mr. Tanaka. You did the packing.

WILFRED
I did, sir.

BELLAMY
What was inside the cat?

WILFRED
Sawdust, sir.

BELLAMY
Only sawdust?

WILFRED
And a few cotton wads. Sir.

BELLAMY
And the eleven stone?

WILFRED
(quietly)
I only lifted the end, sir.

MRS. PRENDERGAST
Wilfred is a good boy.

BELLAMY
I'm sure he is. Miss Vasquez. You are an artist.

MISS VASQUEZ
I am a craftswoman.

BELLAMY
You can tell, I think, the difference between a cat and a man.

MISS VASQUEZ
I can tell the difference between a cat and a lie.

BELLAMY
Which was this?

MISS VASQUEZ
A cat.

BELLAMY
Then open it.

Silence. The stove ticks. Mrs. Prendergast tightens her grip on her handbag. Wilfred stares at the floorboards.

MISS VASQUEZ
It's been sewn shut.

BELLAMY
Cut the stitches.

MRS. PRENDERGAST
Inspector, please. He was a very private man.

BELLAMY
He is a very dead one, madam.

The scalpel catches the lamplight. Bellamy steps forward, and the others half-rise as one. Miss Vasquez raises the blade, Wilfred bolts for the door, and Mrs. Prendergast lunges for the handbag as it slides from her lap.

The stuffed heron topples across the doorway. Wilfred trips over it and falls flat.
